  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find $det(A)-3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,\u27f9\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero row, we obtain:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\u27f9\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-3det(B)=0-3\\cdot 0=0.$",
